  ! #245: "Hovering or focusing a badge shows the source, heading and snippet, so you can check each claim without leaving the answer." - The facts say the tooltip shows title, source › heading, and snippet; the 'check each claim without leaving the answer' benefit is not stated. Also, the first bullet on inline citation badges duplicates the later citations bullet.
  ! #218: "The check runs on every grounded answer, so you no longer depend on the model choosing to run it." - The facts say the check is forced once after retrieval (force-once), not on every grounded answer; it guarantees at least one check after any retrieval, not each answer.
  ! #218: "The assistant now checks each knowledge-base-grounded answer for support in the retrieved sources before it finishes." - The facts say enforcement is force-once after passages appear, and the verdict is not surfaced to users; it is not a per-answer user-visible check.
  ! #219: "Answers that match the sources in meaning are no longer marked as ungrounded for using different wording." - The facts say the semantic path is not deterministic and falls back to lexical scoring without a Voyage key or on embedding failure, so this overstates the guarantee; the verdict is also not surfaced to users.

